  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 614320,
  "published": "2026-06-11T12:46:49.173Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 2.0.12 - Multiple documents with signature tags per signer\n\n**Bug Fixes:**\n- Fixed: SetTagSignaturePosition/SetTagRubricPosition overwrote the previous tag position, so operations created with multiple documents using tags only included the last document. Both methods now accumulate positions, and all referenced documents are included in the operation. New TagSignaturePositions/TagRubricPositions list properties expose them; the singular properties remain for backward compatibility (returning the last added).\n\nVersion 2.0.11 - Shortened Signature URL exposed in OperationCreatedResponseMember\n\n**Improvements:**\n- OperationCreatedResponseMember now exposes ShortenedSignatureUrl (mapped from the API's `shortenedSignatureUrl` field) so integrators can obtain the short URL (https://go.forsign.digital/{code}) returned at operation creation, without parsing the full signature URL.\n\nVersion 2.0.9 - User-Agent Identification\n\n**Improvements:**\n- User-Agent header now includes SDK name and version (ForSign.Sdk/2.0.9) for better API observability\n\nVersion 2.0.8 - Bug Fixes and Validations\n\n**Bug Fixes:**\n- Fixed: GetMemberAttachmentsAsync failed with JsonSerializationException due to incorrect response deserialization (API returns wrapped object, SDK expected raw array)\n- Fixed: Decimal coordinates like \"50.5%\" threw ArgumentException in pt-BR locale due to culture-sensitive float parsing\n- Fixed: AddFileFromUrlAsync silently accepted HTTP error responses (404, 500) and uploaded invalid content as PDF\n\n**Validations:**\n- Form field height minimum enforced at 2% — values below cause rendering issues in signed documents\n- Duplicate form fields (same name and type per member) are now rejected with a clear error message\n\nFor full documentation, visit: https://docs.forsign.digital",
